# Commit Conventions

**When generating commit messages: read [commits.md](../../commits.md). Output MUST be `type: description` – lowercase type + colon + space + description. Never output "Update ..." or "Add ..." without the colon. Always: `update: ...`, `add: ...`, `fix: ...`.**

## Types

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| feat | A new feature |
| fix | Bug fix |
| chore | Non-src/test changes (deps, config) |
| refactor | Code change, no bug/feature |
| docs | Documentation |
| style | Formatting, white-space |
| test | Tests |
| perf | Performance |
| ci | CI |
| build | Build / deps |
| revert | Revert previous |
| add | Add file/function/method/variable |
| remove | Remove file/function/method/variable |
| update | Update existing |
| rename | Rename |
| move | Move |
| copy | Copy |
| security | Vulnerabilities |
| hotfix | Urgent bug fix |

## Examples

```
add: location picker added
update: goal detection logic
fix: ball bouncing off goal zone
```

## Sign-off

Include: `Signed-off-by: @gurkanfikretgunak` in commit footer when applicable.

## Template

Project uses `.gitmessage`. Enable:

```bash
git config commit.template .gitmessage
```
